    <p class="tag">Core Service</p>
    <h1>Visa and Immigration Applications</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Understand which process applies to your situation, and move through it with confidence.</p>

    <p>Entering the Philippines to visit, work, study, invest or join family can involve a range of visa and immigration application requirements. Foreign Immigration Services helps you understand which process applies to your circumstances and manages the application on your behalf where appropriate.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing which visa category may be appropriate to your circumstances</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the documentation your application requires</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration on your behalf, where representation is permitted</li>
      <li>Keeping you informed as your application progresses</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Entering the Philippines for tourism, business or short-term purposes</li>
      <li>Relocating for employment</li>
      <li>Joining a spouse or family member already in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Pursuing education or training</li>
      <li>Other entry or immigration-application circumstances not listed here</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us about your situation and what you are hoping to achieve.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We review your circumstances and explain the process that applies to you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help you prepare and organise the required documentation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>Where applicable, we submit your application and monitor its progress.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A valid passport</li>
      <li>Details of your intended purpose and duration of stay in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Supporting documents relevant to your specific application, such as proof of relationship, employment or education, where applicable</li>
      <li>Any existing immigration records relevant to your case</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Ready to Move Forward?</h2>
      <p>Tell us about your situation and we will explain the process that applies to you.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=visa-applications">Request a Visa Assessment</a></p>
    </div>
